# An archive sets the terms for a partner to use a dataset for academic
# research. The policy requires consent evidence and a completed attribution
# duty. Marketing is prohibited and takes priority over a permission.
# The rules allow one process, prohibit mixed research and marketing, and
# send a process with missing duty evidence for review.
# ODRL 2.2 and DPV 2.3 identifiers are written as RDF names in Logical English.
# Sources https://www.w3.org/TR/odrl-model/
#         https://www.w3.org/TR/odrl-vocab/
#         https://w3id.org/dpv/2.3/dpv/

Use prefix ex with namespace "https://example.org/research-access#".
Use prefix odrl with namespace "http://www.w3.org/ns/odrl/2/".
Use prefix dpv with namespace "https://w3id.org/dpv#".

ex:policy is an odrl:Agreement.
ex:policy has odrl:permission ex:research and ex:policy has odrl:prohibition ex:noMarketing.
ex:policy has odrl:conflict odrl:prohibit.
ex:research is an odrl:Permission and ex:noMarketing is an odrl:Prohibition.
ex:research has odrl:assigner ex:archive and ex:noMarketing has odrl:assigner ex:archive.
ex:research has odrl:assignee ex:partner and ex:noMarketing has odrl:assignee ex:partner.
ex:research has odrl:action odrl:use and ex:noMarketing has odrl:action odrl:use.
ex:research has odrl:target ex:dataset and ex:noMarketing has odrl:target ex:dataset.
ex:research has odrl:constraint ex:academic and ex:research has odrl:constraint ex:consented.
ex:noMarketing has odrl:constraint ex:marketing.
ex:academic is an odrl:Constraint and ex:consented is an odrl:Constraint and ex:marketing is an odrl:Constraint.
ex:academic has odrl:leftOperand dpv:hasPurpose and ex:academic has odrl:operator odrl:eq and ex:academic has odrl:rightOperand dpv:AcademicResearch.
ex:marketing has odrl:leftOperand dpv:hasPurpose and ex:marketing has odrl:operator odrl:eq and ex:marketing has odrl:rightOperand dpv:Marketing.
ex:consented has odrl:leftOperand dpv:hasConsentStatus and ex:consented has odrl:operator odrl:eq and ex:consented has odrl:rightOperand dpv:ConsentGiven.
ex:research has odrl:duty ex:credit.
ex:credit is an odrl:Duty and ex:credit has odrl:action odrl:attribute and ex:credit has odrl:attributedParty ex:archive.

# These are process descriptions and given records of fulfillment.

ex:study is a dpv:Process and ex:mixed is a dpv:Process and ex:pending is a dpv:Process.
ex:consent is a dpv:Consent and ex:consent has dpv:hasConsentStatus dpv:ConsentGiven.
For every X, if X is a dpv:Process then
X has ex:requester ex:partner and X has ex:requestedAction odrl:use and
X has ex:requestedAsset ex:dataset and X has dpv:hasLegalBasis ex:consent.
ex:study has dpv:hasPurpose dpv:AcademicResearch.
ex:mixed has dpv:hasPurpose dpv:AcademicResearch and ex:mixed has dpv:hasPurpose dpv:Marketing.
ex:pending has dpv:hasPurpose dpv:AcademicResearch.
ex:study has ex:fulfilledDuty ex:credit and ex:mixed has ex:fulfilledDuty ex:credit.

# This policy uses exact equality for its three operands. A purpose can have
# several asserted values, and a matching value meets the constraint.

For every X and V, if X has dpv:hasPurpose V then observed(X, dpv:hasPurpose, V).
For every X and C and V,
if X has dpv:hasLegalBasis C and C is a dpv:Consent and C has dpv:hasConsentStatus V
then observed(X, dpv:hasConsentStatus, V).
For every R, if ex:policy has odrl:permission R or ex:policy has odrl:prohibition R then R is a policyRule.
For every X and R and P and A and T,
if X is a dpv:Process and R is a policyRule and
X has ex:requester P and R has odrl:assignee P and
X has ex:requestedAction A and R has odrl:action A and
X has ex:requestedAsset T and R has odrl:target T
then candidate(X, R).
For every X and R and C and P and V,
if candidate(X, R) and R has odrl:constraint C and C has odrl:operator odrl:eq and
C has odrl:leftOperand P and C has odrl:rightOperand V and observed(X, P, V)
then satisfied(X, C).
For every X and R and C,
if candidate(X, R) and R has odrl:constraint C and it is not known that satisfied(X, C)
then unmet(X, R).
For every X and R and D,
if candidate(X, R) and R has odrl:duty D and it is not known that X has ex:fulfilledDuty D
then unmet(X, R).
For every X and R, if candidate(X, R) and it is not known that unmet(X, R) then applies(X, R).

# The explicit conflict strategy gives an applicable prohibition priority.
# Review asks for more evidence where neither outcome can be derived.

For every X and R, if ex:policy has odrl:prohibition R and applies(X, R) then X is prohibited.
For every X and R,
if ex:policy has odrl:conflict odrl:prohibit and ex:policy has odrl:permission R and
applies(X, R) and it is not known that X is prohibited
then X is allowed.
For every X, if X is prohibited then X has ex:decision ex:prohibited.
For every X, if X is allowed then X has ex:decision ex:allowed.
For every X, if X is a dpv:Process and it is not known that X is prohibited and it is not known that X is allowed
then X has ex:decision ex:review.

Find every X and Y such that X has ex:decision Y.
